id: 1905-israel-zangwill-recognizes-that-for
when: 1905
themes: [rhetoric-zionist]
---
## [Israel Zangwill](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Israel_Zangwill) recognizes that for Zionism entails Jews must drive out the Arabs.

... or 'grapple with the problem of a large alien population.' Zangwill was a contemporary and supporter of Herzl until 1902. He supported the idea of Jewish colonization of Palestine ('small population of Arabs and fellahin and wandering, lawless, blackmailing Bedouin tribes'). However, by 1904 he came to realize that Palestine already had a people ('the Sanjak of Jerusalem is twice as thickly populated as the United States'). He  broke away from Zionism and founded an alternative Jewish Territorial Organization, supporting Jewish settlement in a land that was avilable.

